 {"id":"fabro-9495","title":"Publish: skip the project gate on loop-asset-only run PRs (keep the PR — it delivers the tracker close)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-11T21:40:07.217Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-11T21:40:07.217Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"Bookkeeping-only run 01M292T3 (3-line .seeds edit closing fabro-7893 as superseded) opened PR #128 through the full project gate — a Rust build/clippy/test run priced ~15 min worst-case that a tracker-line edit cannot affect. Complements open fabro-9f97 (journal-only diff -> no PR): when the run diff intersects only loop-asset paths (.fabro/, .seeds/), keep the PR but mark it publish-eligible with a gate-skipping label or merge without checks. Acceptance: loop-asset-only run PR merges without the project gate; code-carrying PRs unaffected. Basis: run 01M292T3YZ3B3YXXPT1R7F82XK, PR #128, revisor review .fabro/reviews/develop/01M292T3YZ3B3YXXPT1R7F82XK.md rec 2.","labels":["workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-ac16","title":"Engine: auto-stamp a journal painpoint when a stage's tool output arrives truncated (tool + byte count)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-11T21:40:07.418Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-11T21:40:07.418Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"sd ready returned stdout_truncated:true (28,211 bytes, 200 seeds) to the planner of run 01M292T3 (seq 33), yet the stage journal reported painpoints:[] (seq 62) — the improve loop went blind at the exact moment friction occurred. Demand: when the engine truncates a tool output observed by an agent stage, auto-append a journal painpoint (or run notice) naming tool and byte count; friction capture must not depend on the model noticing its own discomfort. Prior art: closed fabro-176b (post-stage hooks for deterministic painpoint capture) is the mechanism; this adds the truncation trigger. Acceptance: a stage with truncated tool output records a painpoint naming tool + sizes without model cooperation. Basis: run 01M292T3 seq 33 vs seq 62.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-2b7a","title":"Publish: make non-strict generation the default for PR title/body prose (strict-then-retry wastes a call per PR)","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-11T21:40:07.608Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-11T22:21:52.533Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"Worker log 2026-09-11 20:35:38: 'PR content structured generation failed; retrying once without strict JSON output' — the strict-JSON first pass for PR prose is a guaranteed-to-fail round trip (~10-15 s wasted per PR) rescued by the existing non-strict retry. Closed prior art: fabro-c7f7/cd27/46f3/890b (dedicated PR model, retry, deterministic fallback). Demand: default PR prose content to non-strict generation or validate-and-degrade in one step. Acceptance: PR publish performs exactly one LLM call for content on the happy path. Basis: run 01M292T3 worker log 20:35:38Z.","labels":["engine"],"closedAt":"2026-09-11T22:21:52.533Z","closeReason":"duplicate of fabro-41b1 (revisor-filed, same demand, P2): 41b1 kept and enriched with the prior-art chain + acceptance criterion from this seed; basis integrate batch 2026-09-11 ~00:26 Berlin"}
