 {"id":"fabro-020b","title":"Cap loop-churn diffs in evidence.nu to numstat plus first ~30 changed lines","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-11T23:50:03.060Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-12T00:06:02.344Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/evidence.nu, render loop-churn/anomaly files as numstat plus the first ~30 changed lines each; keep full diffs for seed-work files only, preserving the adjudicate-every-loop-file contract via the file list. Evidence: this run's evidence capture was 94,873 bytes — mostly full diffs of changed loop files (.seeds/issues.jsonl hunks embed multi-KB seed bodies) — so it reached the reviewer as a blob-ref marker despite preamble_inline_max_kb=16, forcing a 68.8s reviewer blob-paging detour. Effect: typical capture lands under the reviewer's 16 KB inline ceiling, eliminating the per-cycle blob detour. Supply-side complement to open fabro-3c9d/fabro-8d2c/fabro-9837 (budget-side), not a duplicate of them. Basis: run 01M299PVMSE7Q53ZGPP67AHNMG, workflow version e825d8c827ce15defe0aa57d3586b0f369cab48cc7fe711d526776762f442aa1, commit 6f628c21a79469837da6b9bef63903e5f40c1f65","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-1a35","title":"PROJECT_FACTS: resolve abbreviated crate paths by symbol search, not area-prefix guessing","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-11T23:50:09.484Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-12T00:06:02.268Z","description":"Add one line to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/project-facts.md: crates live under both lib/components/ and lib/foundation/; resolve a seed's abbreviated paths by symbol search (rg -ln <symbol>), never by guessing the area prefix. Evidence: the planner probed the non-existent lib/foundation/fabro-llm/src/... path (events 45-59: two failed rg probes, one fd: command not found, then a symbol search found it) because PROJECT_FACTS names lib/foundation/ as a primary area while fabro-llm lives under lib/components/. Effect: ~3 fewer tool calls and 2-3 fewer model turns per fresh claim (~30-45s). Scope note: the fd-not-installed half is already open seed fabro-0586 (available-binaries line) — do not duplicate it; closed fabro-3d2d landed only dev-loop asset paths, not crate area prefixes. Basis: run 01M299PVMSE7Q53ZGPP67AHNMG, workflow version e825d8c827ce15defe0aa57d3586b0f369cab48cc7fe711d526776762f442aa1, commit 6f628c21a79469837da6b9bef63903e5f40c1f65","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-0607","title":"fabro-llm: 429 reset-deadline prose is parsed as naive-UTC — provider wallclock offsets corrupt the window and can silently disable the park (west-of-UTC)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-11T23:33:41.920Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-11T23:33:41.920Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"PR #131 (run 01M299PVMSE7Q53ZGPP67AHNMG, seed fabro-a3d8) parses the 429 prose 'Your limit will reset at 2026-09-03 05:35:16' via NaiveDateTime::parse_from_str and compares it against UTC-now (gateway.rs parse_reset_deadline + reset_window). The provider timestamp carries NO timezone; treating it as UTC is wrong by the provider's local offset. Observed offset: ZAI sends Beijing wallclock (2026-09-11 incident, handoff fabro-91bf: 'Reset 13:14:50' was Beijing time; user decision 2026-09-12 for fabro-1f70: provider timestamps are timezone-untrustworthy). Consequences: (1) structured provider_retry_after/long_rate_limit_window durations are off by the offset (telemetry + any future consumer scheduling on them); (2) SHARP EDGE: for providers west of UTC the naive-UTC deadline is often in the PAST -> reset_window returns None -> treated as 'window reopened' -> normal short-window retries burn attempts against a live limit -> hard fail instead of park — the exact failure mode a3d8 was built to eliminate. The a3d8 tests only cover UTC-formatted fixtures so this is untested. Demand: naive (offset-less) prose timestamps must never be used as absolute deadlines — options: require an explicit offset (RFC3339) for authoritative windows; otherwise treat the window as UNKNOWN-ETA (fail-fast + park on prose PRESENCE, report window as unbounded, do not compute a duration); optionally calibrate a per-provider offset empirically. Acceptance: tests with a Beijing-offset sample (+8h) and a US-offset sample (-6h, past-deadline case) prove the park still triggers and no negative/None window disables it. Basis: PR #131 diff (gateway.rs lines ~173-194), run 01M299PVMSE7Q53ZGPP67AHNMG, user session 2026-09-12 ~01:35 Berlin.","labels":["engine"]}
